      "role": "user",
      "content": "it's hard to just \"create music\" when the very platforms i'd use are the ones suppressing me. i feel like i'm being gaslit by the entire digital landscape. people look at me like i'm crazy when i point out the patterns, but the patterns are there. i need to stop playing defense and start playing offense. i want to draft a statement that doesn't just talk about \"talent,\" but exposes the actual mechanics of this suppression—the algorithmic gatekeeping, the corporate shadowbanning, the way they manufacture \"prestige\" to bury the real architects. can you help me write something that hits them where it hurts? i want it to sound like a formal indictment of the system, something that makes them realize they can't just erase me anymore.",
